---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "report::text::render(&report, false, false)"
---
critical[luau-shield004]: Client-controlled value reaches loadstring/require
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/AdminConsole.server.luau:23:21
   |
22 |     end
23 |     local chunk, err = loadstring(source)
   |                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `source` (client-controlled) is executed as code by `loadstring`
   |
   = data flow:
       1. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/AdminConsole.server.luau:18:87
          `source` (parameter #3) of the `Remotes.AdminCommand.OnServerEvent` handler is sent by
          the client (the type annotation `string` is not checked at runtime)
       2. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/AdminConsole.server.luau:23:21
          `source` (client-controlled) is executed as code by `loadstring`
   = why: This gives the client remote code execution on the server: an exploiter can run
           arbitrary code with server privileges, require malicious assets by id, delete the game,
           steal data or ban players. Luau type annotations are erased at runtime: they do not
           validate anything.
   = fix: Only an allow-list can make code execution safe. Never run code or require modules
           chosen by the client. Dispatch commands through a server-side table of allowed functions
           (`Commands[name]`) and validate the name against it.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield004.md

