high[luau-shield005]: Client-controlled URL, headers or body in an HttpService request
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/Modules/Analytics.luau:19:14
   |
18 |     })
19 |     HttpService:PostAsync(url, body, Enum.HttpContentType.ApplicationJson)
   |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `url` (client-controlled, from `eventName`) is used in the URL of `HttpService:PostAsync()`
   |
   = data flow:
       1. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/LobbyService.server.luau:37:67
          `eventName` (parameter #2) of the `Remotes.TrackEvent.OnServerEvent` handler is sent by
          the client (the type annotation `string` is not checked at runtime)
       2. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/LobbyService.server.luau:38:2
          passed to `Analytics.track` as `eventName`
       3. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/Modules/Analytics.luau:14:8
          assigned to `url`
       4. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/Modules/Analytics.luau:19:14
          `url` (client-controlled, from `eventName`) is used in the URL of
          `HttpService:PostAsync()`
   = why: The client can make your server send requests to arbitrary endpoints or paths, abuse
           your webhooks and proxies (spam, @everyone pings, Terms of Service violations that get
           the webhook or game banned) and exhaust the HttpService request budget. Luau type
           annotations are erased at runtime: they do not validate anything.
   = fix: The value is not allow-listed, matched against a strict pattern, converted with tonumber
           or encoded with HttpService:UrlEncode. Keep URLs on the server and choose them through
           an allow-listed key. Encode client values with `HttpService:UrlEncode`, convert ids with
           `tonumber`, limit the length of text and rate-limit the remote.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield005.md

