           spends DataStore/HTTP budgets, creates instances or yields, which is enough to lag or
           crash the server and to exhaust request quotas for everyone.
   = fix: Add a per-player cooldown (store `os.clock()` per player and return early when called
           too often), a busy flag while the previous request is running, or a shared rate limiter
           module.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield007.md

low[luau-shield007]: Remote handler does expensive work without a rate limit
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:43:35
   |
42 | -- CFrame of the preview when the player confirms.
43 | Remotes.PlaceObject.OnServerEvent:Connect(function(player: Player, itemId: string, cframe: CFrame)
   |                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the `Remotes.PlaceObject.OnServerEvent` handler calls `template:Clone()` on every request, with no rate limit
   |
   = why: Exploiters can fire a remote thousands of times per second. Without a limit, each call
           spends DataStore/HTTP budgets, creates instances or yields, which is enough to lag or
           crash the server and to exhaust request quotas for everyone.
   = fix: Add a per-player cooldown (store `os.clock()` per player and return early when called
           too often), a busy flag while the previous request is running, or a shared rate limiter
           module.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield007.md

high[luau-shield002]: Client-controlled value assigned to a sensitive Instance property
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:57:9
   |
56 |     local object = template:Clone()
57 |     object:PivotTo(cframe)
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `cframe` (client-controlled) is passed to `object:PivotTo()`
   |
   = data flow:
       1. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:43:84
          `cframe` (parameter #3) of the `Remotes.PlaceObject.OnServerEvent` handler is sent by
          the client (the type annotation `CFrame` is not checked at runtime)
       2. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:57:9
          `cframe` (client-controlled) is passed to `object:PivotTo()`
   = why: The server replicates these properties to everyone. Trusting the client lets exploiters
           teleport, fly, heal themselves, kill other players, move or delete parts, or display
           unfiltered text to other players. Luau type annotations are erased at runtime: they do
           not validate anything.
   = fix: Missing: a lower bound and an upper bound (or a distance check against the character).
           Compute the value on the server (from server-side stats, the character's real position,
           etc.). If it must come from the client, clamp it to a sensible range, check distances
           against the character, allow-list instances, and filter text with TextService.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield002.md

high[luau-shield003]: Instance sent by the client used without checking ownership or location
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:69:9
   |
68 |     end
69 |     object:Destroy()
   |            ^^^^^^^^^ `object:Destroy()` is called on `object`, an Instance chosen by the client
   |
   = data flow:
       1. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:64:69
          `object` (parameter #2) of the `Remotes.DeleteObject.OnServerEvent` handler is sent by
          the client (the type annotation `Model` is not checked at runtime)
       2. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/PlotService.server.luau:69:9
          `object:Destroy()` is called on `object`, an Instance chosen by the client
   = why: A remote can be fired with any Instance the client can see: another player's tool, a
           door on the other side of the map, a part of someone else's plot. Type checks such as
           `IsA` only prove what kind of object it is, not that the player is allowed to touch it.
           Luau type annotations are erased at runtime: they do not validate anything.
   = fix: A type check such as `IsA` only proves what kind of object it is, not that the player
           owns it or may use it. Verify ownership or location before using the Instance:
           `inst:IsDescendantOf(player.Character)`, compare an `Owner` attribute with
           `player.UserId`, check the distance to the character, or look it up in a server-side
           list of allowed instances.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield003.md

