high[luau-shield001]: Client-controlled value written to currency, stats or saved data
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/ShopService.server.luau:43:2
   |
42 |     end
43 |     profile.Inventory[itemId] = true
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `itemId` (client-controlled) chooses which entry of `profile.Inventory` is written
   |
   = data flow:
       1. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/ShopService.server.luau:35:64
          `itemId` (parameter #2) of the `Remotes.BuyItem.OnServerEvent` handler is sent by the
          client (the type annotation `string` is not checked at runtime)
       2. examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/ShopService.server.luau:43:2
          `itemId` (client-controlled) chooses which entry of `profile.Inventory` is written
   = why: Exploiters can fire any remote with any arguments. If the server adds a client-supplied
           amount to a currency, saves a client-supplied table or lets the client pick the
           DataStore key, an exploiter can give themselves unlimited currency, corrupt other
           players' data or poison saves with NaN/huge values. Luau type annotations are erased at
           runtime: they do not validate anything.
   = fix: The key is not checked against an allow-list (or a strict pattern): the client chooses
           which entry is written, for example `Coins` or another player's save. Let the server
           decide amounts (look prices and rewards up in a server table by an allow-listed id). If
           a number must come from the client, check `typeof(x) == "number"`, reject NaN (`x ~= x`)
           and check both bounds before using it. Never use client data as a DataStore key.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield001.md

medium[luau-shield006]: Server waits for a client with RemoteFunction:InvokeClient
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/server/TradeService.server.luau:22:40
   |
21 |     busy[target] = true
22 |     local accepted = Remotes.ConfirmTrade:InvokeClient(target, player.Name, coins)
   |                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^ `Remotes.ConfirmTrade:InvokeClient()` makes the server wait for an answer from a client, which may never come
   |
   = why: A malicious client can simply never return: the server thread yields forever (pcall does
           not help), leaking memory and blocking whatever logic waits for the answer. A client
           that errors or leaves also breaks the call, and every value it returns is
           client-controlled.
   = fix: Use a RemoteEvent for the request and another for the reply (with a server-side
           timeout), or at least run the invoke in a detached thread (`task.spawn`) with a timeout
           and validate the returned values.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield006.md

critical[luau-shield008]: Secret hard-coded in code that replicates to clients
  --> examples/vulnerable-game/src/shared/Config.luau:44:26
   |
43 | Config.AnalyticsUrl = "https://analytics.tycoonshop.example/v1"
44 | Config.AnalyticsApiKey = "tsk_live_4f9a2c7e1b8d3f6a0c5e9b2d7a4f1c8e"
   |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ credential `tsk_live_4f9…` is hard-coded in a ModuleScript replicated to clients: every player can read it
   |
   = why: Exploiters can decompile every LocalScript and replicated ModuleScript. A leaked webhook
           can be spammed or deleted, and a leaked API key gives full access to the account or
           service behind it.
   = fix: Move the secret to the server (ServerScriptService/ServerStorage), store it with Roblox
           secrets (`HttpService:GetSecret`) and revoke the leaked credential.
   = docs: https://github.com/Topogamer0/luau-shield/blob/main/docs/rules/luau-shield008.md

